# Line endings in the working tree: LF, whatever the workstation (#171). The checks compare
# these files, byte for byte, with what a tool writes or with the format they hold: checked
# out in CRLF — `core.autocrlf` on Windows —, they would all look outdated.
#
# - what a tool writes (`generated` in tools/paths.toml): the volumes of the fake back, the
#   listing of the examples, the client of the front, the projection, the inventory;
# - the front, which Prettier checks with LF line endings, catalogues included;
# - the examples of the contract, which the generator of the volumes reads;
# - the originals of the copies the front compares byte for byte: the drawings of docs/assets,
#   whose logos and icon it serves (`src/theme/brand.test.ts`).
#
# `text=auto` leaves a binary file alone. tools/tests/test_gitattributes.py holds the list.
fixtures/** text=auto eol=lf
frontend/** text=auto eol=lf
docs/assets/*.svg text eol=lf
docs/spec/waterfall-spec.md text eol=lf
docs/api/INVENTORY.md text eol=lf
LICENSES/** text eol=lf
**/uv.lock text eol=lf
